The code half is genuinely good and I verified it works rather than reading it: with cost_warn_usd = 5.0 in a temp-dir .yoyo.toml, yoyo config get cost_warn_usd returns 5.0 (.yoyo.toml). All three specified steps landed as designed:

• the reader returns raw text, so parse_cost_threshold stays the one statement of what a valid threshold is (no second parser to diverge);
• `"cost_warn_usd" joined SETTABLE_KEYS **with** its validate_config_value` arm in the same diff, and that arm deliberately *refuses* junk where the config reader is permissive — an asymmetry the code comments and justifies (a human is standing at the /config set door and can be told);
• `resolve_cost_threshold became a flag→env→config chain with the "precedence chain, not an OR" reasoning written at the function, one set_cost_threshold call site, and the AtomicU64+AtomicBool` landmine untouched.

What fails is the half with no gate. The commit is three source files; CLAUDE.md was never opened. It still asserts, verbatim, *"the config key is still owed** and remains the open half of #891, because `cost_warn_usd` needs `src/config.rs` + `SETTABLE_KEYS` + `validate_config_value`"* — every clause of which this diff falsified, sitting in the one file re-injected as authoritative context every session. The register entries are stale the same way (src/cli.rs 6968 vs 6975, src/config.rs 3927 vs 3970), both inside the 100-line grace band, which is exactly why the gate warned and the suite still went green.

That is the mechanism this repo already recorded twice on #864: cargo test cannot fail for a false sentence, the structural gates all answer is the code consistent with itself, and none answers is the prose consistent with the code — so the only readers left are the evaluator and a human. The remedy is small and mechanical: supersede rather than erase the owed-key clause, name the chain and why it is a chain, restate the two limits that did not move (never stops a run; per-process only), and paste the two register numbers from what the gate itself prints after running cargo fmt.
